# Project Rules for the AI Agent (Antigravity)

Project: Proof Keeper (full requirements are in docs/SRS.md).

At the start of EVERY task:
1. Read this file and docs/SRS.md (only the sections named in the task).
2. Only edit the files named in the task. Do not rewrite other people's modules.

Tech: Python 3.11, Streamlit, PyMuPDF, sentence-transformers (all-MiniLM-L6-v2), scikit-learn.
Windows 10/11 laptop, 8 GB RAM, no GPU. Everything must run locally.

Code rules:
- Keep code simple and commented. The developers are students and must understand every line.
- Keep the module structure: modules/pdf_processor.py, text_extractor.py,
  information_extractor.py, similarity_engine.py, evidence_manager.py, storage.py.
- Settings live in config.py. Do not hard-code paths or weights.
- Use type hints and short docstrings.
- Do not add new libraries without telling me and updating requirements.txt.

Safety rules from the SRS (very important):
- NEVER invent facts, quotes, parties, sections or page numbers.
- If something is not found, return "Not found" and show an uncertainty message.
- Always keep page numbers with extracted text.
- Similarity score is NOT legal relevance, NOT a probability, NOT binding precedent.
- Show the stored outcome of similar cases separately from the similarity explanation.
- A bad file must never crash the app. Show a clear error message instead.

After each task:
- Tell me how to run it and how to test it, in simple English.
- List the files you changed.
